Z||000003||BroCar 87||05-23-2000||02:31 PM||||Fieroshop...  I am also painting my car, What type of paint do you use for the heat vents? For experiment, I used the fiero paint out of a can then clearcoated it with heat resistant engine clearcoat. It looked great. Then today i noticed it wasn't lookin to good. I believe the heat got to the paint. It lasted about a week and looked awsome. So my question again... What type of paint should i use. I want it to be black. Should i use acrylic enamel to get it done quick and easy? or go with a base/clear coat??<P>Thanks A Lot in Advance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroshop||05-23-2000||07:17 PM||||BroCar87, As far as the black trim paint I use SEM original black trim paint. This paint last and holds up really well, it has a satin finish which is what the Fieros came with. I have some cans here in stock and I beleive that they are priced around $16.00, but don't quote me. If you call me I will inform you of the price.<BR>I have posted pictures of the blue Ferrarri in another post. Check it out and let me know how you like it.<BR>As far as the paint we use PPG mostly even though we are going to use Sherwin Williams paint for my 88 GT.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 05-23-2000).]||||reg||1
